"Skill Deconstruct is a hidden skill that destroys a skill and gives its template."
"It cannot be revealed, shared or discovered, and the System censors talk of it."
"A template is proportional to the destroyed skill's level; LV 1 gives mere scraps."
"Repeat deconstruction adds to the template; excess past the maximum is thrown away."
"Deconstruction refunds no experience, proficiency or points, and cannot be undone."
"Its prompt warns \"Warning: this cannot be undone.\" and that sub-skills go too."
"A deconstructed skill must be bought again to be deconstructed again."
"Traits cannot be deconstructed; no Trait Deconstruct exists."
"Skills that touch the System interface give interface lore only when stripped bare."
"Deconstructed knowledge lets one rebuild skills as spells and buy related skills early."
"Elemental Praxis is a hidden quest skill; it cannot be revealed, shared or deconstructed."
"Mana Dominion has no levels and gives no System guidance: its user shapes Mana freely."
"Mana Dominion cannot be shared or deconstructed, and needs Mother's approval to reach."
"Gramps builds open-ended traits and tests them on his [Experiments]."
"Chimeric Mimicry, the trait-borrowing gift, was made by Gramps himself."
"Chimeric Mimicry LV 9 gives a budget of 81 points for borrowed traits, capped at LV 9."
"Split Personality turns acted personas into real selves who can hold their own classes."
"Skills given to a split persona are lost for good; they can never be taken back."
"The System once renamed a trait after a slime kept trying to buy it against the rules."
